DocumentName: handheld-multi-modal
DocumentNamespace: https://github.com/open-edge-platform/federal-and-aerospace-ai-suite/tree/main/handheld-multi-modal
Creator: Organization: Intel Corporation
Creator: Tool: manual-curation
Created: 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z
CreatorComment: <text>
SPDX SBOM for the handheld-multi-modal application
(federal-and-aerospace-ai-suite/handheld-multi-modal), v2 operator console.

Scope: third-party open-source components consumed by the application —
container images referenced by compose/handheld-multi-modal.yaml and
compose/cameras.yaml, the base image and Python pip dependencies of the
locally built backend service (backend/Dockerfile, backend/requirements.txt),
and the AI models deployed by the stack (config/chatqna/models.lock.json,
config/model-download/yolo26s.json). Only direct, pinned pip requirements are
listed; their transitive dependencies are not enumerated. Models that are
not deployed are not listed.

Intel-authored sources in this repository (including the handheld/backend
image built from backend/) are NOT enumerated as packages; only third-party
dependencies are listed, per the SBOM request.
</text>

##############################################################################
# Top-level package describing the application itself
##############################################################################

PackageName: handheld-multi-modal
SPDXID: SPDXRef-Package-handheld-multi-modal
PackageVersion: 2026.2
PackageSupplier: Organization: Intel Corporation
PackageDownloadLocation: https://github.com/open-edge-platform/federal-and-aerospace-ai-suite
PackageHomePage: https://github.com/open-edge-platform/federal-and-aerospace-ai-suite/tree/main/handheld-multi-modal
FilesAnalyzed: false
PackageLicenseConcluded: Apache-2.0
PackageLicenseDeclared: Apache-2.0
PackageCopyrightText: <text>Copyright (C) 2026 Intel Corporation</text>
PackageSummary: <text>Local operator console for handheld edge devices built from Open Edge Platform 2026.2.0 containers and a FastAPI backend: live camera analytics with DL Streamer Pipeline Server, evidence history, mission documents via Chat Q&A, alerts, speech-to-text and text-to-speech, and hardware telemetry, packaged as a Docker Compose deployment.</text>

Relationship: SPDXRef-DOCUMENT DESCRIBES SPDXRef-Package-handheld-multi-modal


